// read_line() at EOF with no data is a RUNTIME error (DEC-020, research/028
// M3): `end of input`. The harness gives the program stdin=/dev/null (or a
// closed stdin), which is an immediate, deterministic EOF — so the first
// read_line() fails before it can read a byte. This is the pin for the
// EOF-without-data contract: a real line (the positive case) lives in the
// selfhost/io_gate_stdin.sh gate, where stdin is redirected from a fixture
// (conformance has no stdin to give).
// EXPECT-RUNTIME-ERROR: end of input
fn main() {
    print("before")
    print(read_line())
    print("after")
}
